 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "While pair programming can have its advantages, I want you to develop your own style and thinking process first.",
  "It's important to establish your own coding habits and instincts without being influenced too much by your colleagues.",
  "Synchronous for those urgent matters and quick questions, and asynchronous for more thoughtful discussions and updates.",
  "It's all about finding that balance between being responsive and giving your colleagues the space to concentrate.",
  "Another aspect of remote work is managing your own time and energy effectively.",
  "Setting a schedule, taking breaks, and maintaining a healthy work-life balance are all part of the equation.",
  "It's a common pitfall, and it's important to set boundaries.",
  "Try to stick to a consistent schedule as much as possible and communicate your working hours to the team.",
  "Even if it's just a corner of your room, try to separate your work area from your living space as much as possible.",
  "It helps you mentally transition into \"work mode\" and also allows you to \"leave work\" at the end of the day.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of including try statements in our functions to handle potential exceptions gracefully.",
  "It's a small detail, but it makes our code more robust and easier to debug.",
  "Let's start all our variable names with 'y_'.",
  "Not for now.",
  "Just remember, consistency and clarity are key when it comes to coding standards.",
  "And don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about remote work or coding practices.",
  "It's essential for driving results and achieving our goals."
 ],
